message: "If ContextMesh or one of its Reality Probes materially supports your work, please cite this repository and the specific probe artifact you used."
title: "ContextMesh: Reality-first full-coverage context verification"
type: software
version: 0.15.0
date-released: 2026-09-26
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/hippoley/ContextMesh"
url: "https://github.com/hippoley/ContextMesh"
authors:
  - name: "ContextMesh contributors"
keywords:
  - context verification
  - RAG evaluation
  - LLM evaluation
  - AI agents
  - retrieval
  - provenance
  - long context
  - agent memory
  - observability
  - evidence lifecycle
abstract: >-
  ContextMesh is a reality-first context-verification runtime and public
  correctness lab for AI systems. It tracks where decisive evidence stops
  participating across ingestion, storage, retrieval, eligibility, rendering,
  model visibility, authority, and final judgment. Reality Probes pin external
  system versions, reproduce narrow failure mechanisms, and publish executable
  before/after evidence, including results that falsify ContextMesh's own claims.
